    "created_at": "2022-04-07T09:46:01Z",
    "updated_at": "2022-04-07T09:46:01Z",
    "body": "> Chrome ignores registerProtocolHandler requests if they are not issued by user gestures. In chrome, this is evaluated based on the frame's [UserActivation](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/interaction.html#tracking-user-activation) state.\r\n> \r\n> I believe that Firefox has the same requirement.\r\n\r\nI am curious why you believe this? I don't think we do... cf. https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=668577 and all the complaints from office365 users when they started calling `registerProtocolHandler` willy-nilly on page load.",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
