    "body": "Would be a valid solution to throw an exception if the registerProtocolHandler request has been instantiated without any user gesture ? That would make easier to define WPT for this requirement; assuming we agreed on add it explicitly to the spec. We could, for instance, use [test_driver.bless](https://web-platform-tests.org/writing-tests/testdriver.html#test_driver.bless) in a similar way than in the [show-picker-user-gesture.html](https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt/blob/master/html/semantics/forms/the-input-element/show-picker-user-gesture.html) test.\r\n\r\nLooking at the available [DomException error names](https://webidl.spec.whatwg.org/#idl-DOMException-error-names) we could, perhaps, use [InvalidStateError](https://webidl.spec.whatwg.org/#invalidstateerror); I guess [NotAllowedError](https://webidl.spec.whatwg.org/#notallowederror) would perhaps fit better on this use case, but it doesn't have a code name and value, which is useful to define the asserts in the tests.",
